### Article 34. Professional training

1. Professional training - acquisition and improvement of professional knowledge, abilities and skills by a person in accordance with his vocation and abilities, which ensures the appropriate level of professional (full or partial) qualification, competence for professional activity and competitiveness in the labor market.

__

2. The professional training system includes:

1) persons undergoing initial professional training in educational institutions and other institutions that provide or provide training for qualified workers and specialists;

2) employees who undergo initial professional training, retraining and advanced training in the course of work;

3) unemployed people who are looking for work and need initial professional training, retraining or advanced training.

3. Increasing the competitiveness of employees on the labor market in accordance with the requirements of modern production and the service sector is carried out by ensuring the effective functioning and development of the system of professional training of employees, assisting in their professional training, retraining and advanced training at enterprises, institutions and organizations, regardless of the form of ownership ,

