Article . Fee for issuing or extending the validity of a permit

1. The fee for issuing a permit is:

1) for permits issued for a period of up to six months, inclusive - three subsistence minimums for able-bodied persons, established by law on January 1 of the calendar year in which the employer or his authorized person submitted the documents;

2) for permits issued for a period of six months to one year inclusive - five subsistence minimums for able-bodied persons established by law on January 1 of the calendar year in which the employer or his authorized person submitted the documents;

