### Article 46. Suitable work for the unemployed

##### 1. A job that simultaneously:

1) corresponds to his education, profession/professions (specialties/specialties), qualification, as well as work experience acquired by the person during his employment. When offering a suitable job, the duration of work by profession (the profession of the corresponding group if there are skills), specialty, qualification, experience, duration of unemployment, as well as the need of the labor market are taken into account;

2) takes into account the transport accessibility established by the order of the head of the local state administration or the decision of the executive body of the relevant council. A job is considered suitable if the travel time and distance to the place of work (one-way), where daily transportation is organized, for the unemployed who are employed under the following conditions:

full-time - does not exceed an hour and a half and 60 kilometers;

part-time - does not exceed one hour and 40 kilometers;

3) corresponds to the wage level depending on the duration of unemployment. When selecting a suitable job, the following salary is taken into account:

not lower than the amount of salary (income, financial support) at the last place of work (service), and for persons who are in the status of registered unemployed - within 90 calendar days from the date of granting the status of registered unemployed;

60 percent of the salary (income, financial support) at the last place of work (service) - for persons who are in the status of registered unemployed from the 91st to the 180th calendar day;

minimum wage for full-time work (day) for persons who:

are unemployed for more than 180 calendar days;

wish to resume work after a long (

 of work (service) - for persons who are in the status of registered unemployed from the 91st to the 180th calendar day;

minimum wage for full-time work (day) for persons who:

are unemployed for more than 180 calendar days;

wish to resume work after a long (more than 12 months) break;

search for work for the first time;

while being in the status of registered unemployed, received a new profession at the direction of the territorial body of the central executive body, which implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration (according to the received new profession).

2. For persons who do not have a profession (specialty) and are looking for a job for the first time, work that does not require professional training or work that requires initial professional training, in particular directly at the workplace, is considered suitable.

For persons who wish to resume work after a break of more than 12 months, the work they performed at their last place of work (service), or work in previously acquired professions (specialties), or work with preliminary retraining in a new profession is considered suitable (specialty) and/or advanced training at the direction of the territorial body of the central executive body that implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration, taking into account the needs of the labor market.

3. The selection of a suitable job is carried out by a career counselor among the vacancies submitted by the employer in accordance with the second paragraph of the fourth paragraph of the third part of Article 50 of this Law, as well as current vacancies obtained from other sources (in particular, from job search information resources) and included in the Unified information and analytical system of the central body of executive power, which implements state policy in the field of population employment and labor migration.

The selection of suitable work for persons with disabilities is carried out taking into account the provisions of the Law of Ukraine "On the Basics of Social Protection of Persons with Disabilities in Ukraine

